# Chimney stack (SOLID, 16x16; Brunnwinkl house 4's eave step): fieldstone
# masonry i/m with a w lit left edge and m/d right edge, a light stone cap
# slab on top (the standing surface: w lip, like the other solid tiles) over
# the dark d smoke opening between two short posts. No smoke drawn: the
# collision is exactly the 16x16 cell (D-038 drawn = solid).
# Autotiled vertically (D-020 mask; 1 = same tile above, 4 = below; the
# left/right bits are ignored): only the top of a stack gets the cap, only
# the bottom gets the d base course where it meets the roof, so a stack of 2
# reads as one chimney. Generated by the pixel-artist with a throwaway
# script; the grids below are the source.
sprite = tile_chimney
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
---
frame auto 0
